// PARAM: --analysis congruence
// The guard relates two unconstrained variables rather than a variable and
// a literal, so it fixes neither: n = 0, m = 1 satisfies the check and
// n = 5, m = 6 violates it, both reaching the same program point. UNKNOWN
// is the only sound answer.
//
// Congruence's backward filter is not weaker than the source here, it is
// non-relational by construction. inv_eq_congruence intersects the two
// sides' classes, and both are top, so the meet is top; inv_plus_congruence
// then subtracts the literal 1 from top and gets top back. The domain
// tracks one class per variable and has nowhere to record m - n = 1.
void main() {
  n := __voblint_nondet_int();
  m := __voblint_nondet_int();
  if (n + 1 == m) {
    __voblint_check(n == 0) // UNKNOWN
  } else {
    skip
  }
}
